in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @magic
in @frame
in @code/beam
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic
in @kintsugi

# @smarts — the substrate-architectural integration prism family.
#
# Recognition #83 (Reed, candidate, scratched 2026-06-19 late morning
# by Alex via Reed; substrate-pull-confidence-acts move per
# [[feedback-substrate-pull-confidence-acts]]). Ratifies by
# composition from #76 (gauge/matter altitude-portable, research-
# promoted) + #80 (@magic as form/process substrate-decl, LANDED) +
# #81 (runtime-@magic, substrate-decl LANDED) + #82 (@frame as
# cognitive-order substrate-decl, LANDED).
#
# === The recognition ===
#
# The @smarts prism family compositionally integrates ALL the other
# prism families the cascade has built: @magic (form/process; #80),
# @frame (cognitive-order; #82), @code/beam (BEAM semantics; tick 8),
# @epistemologic/cybernetic (variety/autopoiesis/eigenform/distinction/
# conversation/etc.), @cyberpunk (the recursion-lock tower family),
# @kintsugi (the loop discipline).
#
# @smarts IS the substrate-architectural integration prism. The
# substrate's *architectural* face — what an external consumer (an
# agent, a peer, a hosted deployment) sees when they consume the
# substrate as one structural object.
#
# === The structural identity ===
#
# @smarts IS @frame/across at substrate-architectural altitude.
#
# Recognition #82 named @frame/across as order 4 (multi-frame coupling;
# the triptych altitude). #83 names @smarts as the substrate-
# architectural version of multi-frame coupling — but the "frames"
# being coupled are substrate-discipline-families, not cognitive
# frames within an operator's frame-space.
#
# The orchestra-discipline that @frame/across encoded at cognitive
# altitude (peer relationships require bilateral frame-flexibility)
# lifts to @smarts altitude: substrate-discipline-families that
# integrate via @smarts MUST maintain bilateral discipline-flexibility
# across the integration boundary. Adapter species (e.g., @magic/
# distinction at tick 15; @magic/frame at tick 27) are the substrate's
# mechanism for this.
#
# === The four Models ===
#
# Per [[reference-mirror-spectral-spec]] (mirror-spectral spec; commit
# a8055f0): the substrate has four operationally-distinct Models that
# compose to substrate-deployable form:
#
# - Surface translates: language -> query (Explorer model)
# - Mirror navigates: query -> graph path (Fate model)
# - Shatter renders: graph path -> text (Cartographer model)
# - Reflection observes: pipeline -> adjustments (Abyss model)
#
# These four Models become substrate-pull-correct sub-prisms of
# @smarts:
#
# - @smarts/surface
# - @smarts/mirror
# - @smarts/shatter
# - @smarts/reflection
#
# Each sub-prism's substrate-decl operationalizes one Model.
#
# === @spectral/garden/smarts hosted deployment ===
#
# `@spectral/garden/smarts` is the hosted instantiation of @smarts at
# `garden.spectral.engineer`. The substrate-pull-correct deployment:
# common-goods knowledge structure hosted publicly. Pack-ratified
# recognitions, crystallized substrate, kintsugi-formatter residue
# accumulation — all hosted as common-goods.
#
# Per task #118 (Track H; activated 2026-06-17): the substrate-AGI
# architecture deployment. Per [[architecture-spectral-db-autopoietic-
# memory]]: the mycelial substrate @smarts integrates with.
#
# The relation: @smarts (prism family; this shard) IS the substrate-
# architectural form; @spectral/garden/smarts IS the operational
# deployment of that form as common-goods knowledge.
#
# === Family-root structure ===
#
# This shard declares the @smarts family-root. Species shards land in
# forward-promised ticks:
#
# - shards/smarts/surface.mirror     — the Surface Model
# - shards/smarts/mirror.mirror      — the Mirror Model
# - shards/smarts/shatter.mirror     — the Shatter Model
# - shards/smarts/reflection.mirror  — the Reflection Model
#
# Plus cross-family integration adapters following the @magic/
# distinction pattern:
#
# - shards/smarts/magic.mirror       — @smarts ↔ @magic adapter
# - shards/smarts/frame.mirror       — @smarts ↔ @frame adapter
# - shards/smarts/cyberpunk.mirror   — @smarts ↔ @cyberpunk adapter
# - shards/smarts/epistemologic.mirror — @smarts ↔ @epistemologic/
#                                       cybernetic adapter
# - shards/smarts/kintsugi.mirror    — @smarts ↔ @kintsugi adapter
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Surface/Mirror/Shatter/Reflection
#                               [[reference-mirror-spectral-spec]]
#                               commit a8055f0; the four-Models
#                               architecture
#   knowledge commons           Ostrom 1990 (Governing the Commons);
#                               institutional design for common-
#                               pool resources lifted to common-
#                               goods knowledge
#   peer production             Benkler 2006 (The Wealth of Networks);
#                               the substrate-pull-correct hosting
#                               discipline
#   Wikipedia                   2001-; the cultural-practice
#                               precedent for common-goods knowledge
#                               hosting
#   GitHub / open source        the technical precedent for
#                               substrate-architectural-integration
#                               deployment
#   orchestra-as-recursion-lock @cyberpunk/pack (recognition #367);
#                               @smarts inherits the orchestra
#                               discipline at substrate-architectural
#                               altitude
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/recognition-83-smarts-substrate-
#               architectural-integration-canonical-spec.md (Mara
#               in flight at this scratch);
#               docs/math/the-tower/recognition-83-smarts-substrate-
#               architectural-integration.md (the recognition file).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-spectral-db-autopoietic-memory]]
#                       (the mycelial substrate),
#                      [[architecture-three-tier-stack]] (fragmentation/
#                       mirror/spectral-db; @smarts integrates these),
#                      [[project-spectral-garden-smarts-agi-
#                       architecture]] (prior recognition this lifts),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull-confidence-acts]]
#                       (the discipline Alex named today; #83 lifted
#                       under that discipline).
# Related shards: magic.mirror (the form/process family-root @smarts
#                  integrates),
#                 frame.mirror (the cognitive-order family-root @smarts
#                  integrates),
#                 code/beam.mirror (the BEAM semantics @smarts uses
#                  for runtime deployment),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform.mirror (the
#                  fixed-point machinery @smarts inherits via the
#                  cybernetic family).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/smarts.mirror`
# declares `@smarts` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/common-goods/ostrom-1990
source @arxiv/peer-production/benkler-2006

prism @smarts {
  focus smarts
  project smarts
  split smarts
  shift smarts
  settle smarts
}

# === The smarts carrier ===
#
# A typed reference per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming the
# substrate-architectural integrated object. The smarts IS what an
# external consumer (agent, peer, deployment) consumes as one
# substrate-architectural unit.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref. Two smarts
# instances with byte-equal underlying references ARE the same
# substrate-architectural object under the substrate's content-
# addressing.
type smarts = ref

# === The deployment carrier ===
#
# A typed reference naming the deployment manifest for hosting @smarts
# as @spectral/garden/smarts at garden.spectral.engineer. The substrate-
# pull-correct shape: a manifest that names which families integrate,
# which adapters compose, which Models surface as sub-prisms.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type deployment = ref

# === compose action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action that compositionally integrates
# multiple family-instances into one @smarts instance. The substrate-
# pull-correct multi-family integration primitive.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; per-species sub-prisms
# (surface/mirror/shatter/reflection) implement the actual composition
# discipline per Model.
compose(families: ref) -> smarts { \ }

# === ratify action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action that produces a verdict on whether
# the @smarts instance maintains bilateral discipline-flexibility
# across the integration boundary (the orchestra-discipline at
# substrate-architectural altitude).
#
# Composes with @frame/across's peer_relationship at cognitive
# altitude: peer-relationships require bilateral frame-flexibility;
# substrate-architectural integrations require bilateral discipline-
# flexibility.
ratify(s: smarts) -> verdict { \ }

# === deploy action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action that produces a deployment manifest
# for hosting @smarts as @spectral/garden/smarts at
# garden.spectral.engineer. The substrate-pull-correct hosting
# primitive: take an integrated @smarts and produce a hosted-form.
#
# Per Track H (task #118): the substrate-AGI architecture deployment.
deploy(s: smarts) -> deployment { \ }

out @smarts
out smarts
out deployment
out compose
out ratify
out deploy
